  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Phenyl magnesium bromide is called Grignard reagent. One mole of this&nbsp;react with carbonyl compound to give alcohols. It react with aldehyde to form secondary alcohol while with ketones gives tertiary alcohols. The given compound is a tertiary alcohol so, reactant should be a ketone.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/b9aa592f-226f-4376-b5d0-50fd57d5be83-image.png\" style=\"width: 326px; height: 100px;\" /></p></blockquote>",
